Source: secubox-ad-guard
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: SecuBox <dev@secubox.local>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: secubox-ad-guard
Architecture: all
# dns-root-data EST INDISPENSABLE AVEC unbound (#1294).
# Le paquet Debian unbound livre root-auto-trust-anchor-file.conf, qui
# exige /var/lib/unbound/root.key. Cette ancre vient de dns-root-data,
# que unbound RECOMMANDE sans l'exiger — et la construction d'image
# installe avec --no-install-recommends. Resultat sur une image trixie
# fraiche : unbound boucle en echec (26 redemarrages constates) et le
# systeme n'a AUCUNE resolution DNS, alors qu'unbound-anchor, l'outil
# qui sait semer l'ancre, n'est pas installe non plus.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, secubox-core (>= 1.4.0), secubox-toolbox,
 unbound, python3-httpx | python3-pip,
         dns-root-data
Description: SecuBox Ad Guard Module
 Ad and tracker detection with per-device statistics.
 Features blocklist management, delayed blacklisting workflow,
 and device-type classification (IoT, phones, smart TVs, etc.).
 .
 Provides a board-wide DNS ad/tracker sinkhole (#740): compiles the modular
 filter-list resource (EasyList/EasyPrivacy/OISD/HaGeZi/NoScript) and renders
 it as Unbound always_nxdomain local-zones, refreshed weekly by timer.
